  "body": " Workplace Drug Testing and Conditional Probability   An logistics company uses a rapid oral fluid screening test to determine whether machine operators have controlled substances in their system. The rapid screening kit is not totally reliable:  of employees who have not consumed a controlled substance give a false-positive reading (the test indicates drug presence).  of employees who have consumed a controlled substance give a false-negative reading (the test indicates no drug presence).  Suppose that, in fact, of the applicant pool has consumed a controlled substance, and the safety manager tests an employee at random.  Match each conditional probability question on the left with its correct calculated value on the right. Note that there are extra numbers on the right that do not match either scenario!      Find the probability that the employee has consumed the substance, given that the test reading is positive.        Find the probability that the employee has not consumed the substance, given that the test reading is negative.                    Let be the event the drug is present, and be a positive test. Organize your components first: , , and . Use the Law of Total Probability to find the baseline denominators and before finalizing your Bayes' Theorem matrices.    "
