  "body": " The Weighted Collectible Die Experiment   A tabletop gaming store owner purchases an unverified chest containing a total of 16 identical-looking custom, collectible d20 (20-sided) gaming dice. Within the chest, 11 are authentic factory originals that are perfectly balanced and fair, landing on the maximum critical hit symbol exactly 5% of the time. The remaining 5 dice are counterfeit, weighted so that they land on the critical hit symbol with a probability of .      Suppose the store owner reaches into the chest, picks exactly one die completely at random, and rolls it once. What is the probability that the die lands on the critical hit symbol?        Suppose the store owner picks a die completely at random and rolls it once, and it lands on a critical hit. Given this outcome, what is the probability that the dice is one of the counterfeits?        Suppose the store owner picks a die completely at random and rolls that same exact die three times in a row, and it lands on a critical hit every time. Given this consecutive streak, what is the probability that the dice is one of the counterfeits?     "
